korgwm for Debian
=================

This package provides korgwm, a tiling window manager for X11 written in Perl.

Configuration
-------------
An example configuration is available in
/usr/share/doc/korgwm/examples/korgwm.conf.sample.  Copy it to
~/.config/korgwm/korgwm.conf and customise as needed.

korgwm searches for configuration files in the following order, merging
each one it finds:

  /etc/korgwm/korgwm.conf
  /usr/local/etc/korgwm/korgwm.conf
  ~/.korgwmrc
  ~/.config/korgwm/korgwm.conf

Note that the merge is shallow: if you override a section such as `hotkeys`
or `rules`, specify the whole section.

Multi-monitor setup
-------------------
The default `randr_cmd` is

  korgwm_xrandr || xrandr --auto

`korgwm_xrandr` is a user-provided script that korgwm looks up in PATH to
lay out monitors on every RandR event; when it is absent, `xrandr --auto`
is used and you may see "korgwm_xrandr: not found" on stderr.  A working
example is shipped as

  /usr/share/doc/korgwm/examples/korgwm_xrandr

Copy it to ~/bin/korgwm_xrandr, adapt the output names to your hardware
and make it executable.  See also /usr/share/doc/korgwm/Screen_Management.md
in the upstream sources.

Session configuration
---------------------
To start korgwm from a display manager (lightdm, gdm, sddm), select the
"korgwm" session at login.  The korgwm-session wrapper sets up the
environment (XDG, NO_AT_BRIDGE, Java non-reparenting hint, keyboard layout)
and then executes korgwm.

Starting from .xinitrc
----------------------
To start korgwm manually from a text console:

    korgwm-session

or, without the wrapper:

    korgwm

Documentation
-------------
Manual pages: korgwm(1) and korgwm-session(1).

Perl POD is available through perldoc:

    perldoc X11::korgwm

Upstream documentation, including API.md and doc/Screen_Management.md, is
available from https://github.com/zhmylove/korgwm.

Dependencies
------------
X11 libraries: libxcb, libxinerama, libxrandr
Perl modules: AnyEvent, AnyEvent::DBus (libanyevent-dbus-perl), Net::DBus,
              Gtk3, Glib::Object::Introspection, YAML::Tiny, X11::XCB

Bug reporting
-------------
Please report bugs to the Debian Bug Tracking System, or upstream at
https://github.com/zhmylove/korgwm/issues
